    "comment": {
      "comments": [
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12333871/comment/12381457",
          "id": "12381457",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=becke%40u.washington.edu",
            "name": "becke@u.washington.edu",
            "key": "becke@u.washington.edu",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Michael Becke",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "body": "I'm wondering if we should change licenses in mid release.  I do not know if 2.0 causes any \nproblems for users, but it seems like a pretty big change for this release.  Perhaps we can wait until \nafter 2.0 is released.  How does everyone feel about this?\n\nMike",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=becke%40u.washington.edu",
            "name": "becke@u.washington.edu",
            "key": "becke@u.washington.edu",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Michael Becke",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "created": "2004-02-03T11:00:27.000+0000",
          "updated": "2004-02-03T11:00:27.000+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12333871/comment/12381458",
          "id": "12381458",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=oglueck",
            "name": "oglueck",
            "key": "oglueck",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Ortwin Glueck",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Zurich"
          },
          "body": "The problem is, that HttpClient will be *implicitly* licensed under the new\nlicense. So we will cause less confusion if we directly include the new lincense\nnow. See www.apache.org/licenses :\n\n\"All packages produced by the ASF are implicitly licensed under the Apache\nLicense, version 2.0, unless otherwise explicitly stated.\"",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=oglueck",
            "name": "oglueck",
            "key": "oglueck",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Ortwin Glueck",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Zurich"
          },
          "created": "2004-02-03T14:56:08.000+0000",
          "updated": "2004-02-03T14:56:08.000+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12333871/comment/12381459",
          "id": "12381459",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=adrian%40ephox.com",
            "name": "adrian@ephox.com",
            "key": "adrian@ephox.com",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Adrian Sutton",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "body": "The license at the top of the file is the explicit statement that paragraph has an exception for.  So if we \nwere to release 2.0 as is, it would be under the 1.0 license.  I think if we are considering putting out a \nrelease under the 1.0 license we should get approval from the PMC.  Personally, I would release under \nthe 2.0 license.",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=adrian%40ephox.com",
            "name": "adrian@ephox.com",
            "key": "adrian@ephox.com",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Adrian Sutton",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "created": "2004-02-03T15:12:57.000+0000",
          "updated": "2004-02-03T15:12:57.000+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12333871/comment/12381460",
          "id": "12381460",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=oglueck",
            "name": "oglueck",
            "key": "oglueck",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Ortwin Glueck",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Zurich"
          },
          "body": "Roy Fielding states:\n\nWhen modifying the copyright notice for Apache software, the name\nof the copyright owner must be stated as in the following examples:\n\n   Copyright 2004 The Apache Software Foundation.\nor\n   Copyright 2002-2004 The Apache Software Foundation.\nor\n   Copyright 2002,2004 The Apache Software Foundation.\n\nThat is the official name of the corporation as registered in Delaware,\nso it is important not to leave out the \"The\" for the copyright notice\n(just about everywhere else it doesn't matter). ",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=oglueck",
            "name": "oglueck",
            "key": "oglueck",
